            <div id="panel-352bb674-60d3-4c09-9215-e25ae84d8684-1" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-352bb674-60d3-4c09-9215-e25ae84d8684-1" aria-expanded="true" hidden="false">
              <div>


<div class="aem-Grid aem-Grid--12 aem-Grid--default--12 ">
    
    <div class="quick-links white aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--12">

<article class="jpmc-quick-links variant-two ">
    

    <section class="quick-links__card-container">
        <div class="quick-links-card">
            <div class="quick-links-card-details">
                <div class='title'><h3>Long-Context Long-Form Question Answering for Legal Domain</h3>
</div>
                <div class='description'>
                    <p><span class="accented-text">March 2026</span></p>
<p>Legal documents have complex document layouts involving multiple nested sections, lengthy footnotes and further use specialized linguistic devices like intricate syntax and domain-specific vocabulary to ensure precision and authority. These inherent characteristics of legal documents make question answering challenging. In this paper, we address the challenges of long-context question answering in context of long-form answers given the idiosyncrasies of legal documents.</p>
</div>
            </div>

            
                
    <a aria-label="Long-Context Long-Form Question Answering for Legal Domain, learn more" class="link" data-cmp-clickable data-cmp-data-layer="{&#34;event&#34;:&#34;cmp:click&#34;,&#34;webInteraction&#34;:{&#34;ctaType&#34;:&#34;link&#34;,&#34;ctaText&#34;:&#34;Read more&#34;,&#34;ctaUrl&#34;:&#34;https://aclanthology.org/2026.eacl-industry.54/&#34;,&#34;ctaTitle&#34;:&#34;Long-Context Long-Form Question Answering for Legal Domain&#34;,&#34;ctaComponentName&#34;:&#34;Quick Links&#34;}}" href="https://aclanthology.org/2026.eacl-industry.54/" target="_blank">
        <span class="link-text">Read more</span>

        
            
  
  
  <span class="icon icon-16" data-icon="&#xf061"></span>
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  

        
    </a>

            
        </div>
    
        <div class="quick-links-card">
            <div class="quick-links-card-details">
                <div class='title'><h3>MM-BizRAG: Rethinking Multimodal Retrieval-Augmented Generation for General Purpose Enterprise Q&amp;A</h3>
</div>
                <div class='description'>
                    <p><span class="accented-text">July 2026</span></p>
<p>Recent advances in multimodal retrieval-augmented generation (MM-RAG) have shifted toward minimal parsing, relying on page-level images for producing retriever embeddings and for answer generation. While efficient, this trend often neglects explicit handling of the rich, structured information in complex enterprise documents, instead depending on pre-trained embeddings or vision-language models to implicitly capture such structure. In this work, we take a more direct approach: MM-BizRAG proactively extracts and represents document structure via a document structure-aware split that dynamically routes documents through orientation-specific ingestion pipelines, applying explicit layout-aware parsing for vertically structured documents (e.g., reports) and holistic page-level representations for horizontally structured documents (e.g., slide decks).</p>
</div>
            </div>

            
                
    <a aria-label="MM-BizRAG: Rethinking Multimodal Retrieval-Augmented Generation for General Purpose Enterprise Q&amp;A, learn more" class="link" data-cmp-clickable data-cmp-data-layer="{&#34;event&#34;:&#34;cmp:click&#34;,&#34;webInteraction&#34;:{&#34;ctaType&#34;:&#34;link&#34;,&#34;ctaText&#34;:&#34;Read more&#34;,&#34;ctaUrl&#34;:&#34;https://aclanthology.org/2026.acl-industry.134/&#34;,&#34;ctaTitle&#34;:&#34;MM-BizRAG: Rethinking Multimodal Retrieval-Augmented Generation for General Purpose Enterprise Q&amp;A&#34;,&#34;ctaComponentName&#34;:&#34;Quick Links&#34;}}" href="https://aclanthology.org/2026.acl-industry.134/" target="_blank">
        <span class="link-text">Read more</span>

        
            
  
  
  <span class="icon icon-16" data-icon="&#xf061"></span>
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  

        
    </a>

            
        </div>
    </section>
</article>

</div>

    
</div>
</div>
            </div>
            
          
            
            <div id="panel-352bb674-60d3-4c09-9215-e25ae84d8684-2" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-352bb674-60d3-4c09-9215-e25ae84d8684-2" aria-expanded="false" hidden="true">
              <div>


<div class="aem-Grid aem-Grid--12 aem-Grid--default--12 ">
    
    <div class="quick-links white aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--12">

<article class="jpmc-quick-links variant-three ">
    

    <section class="quick-links__card-container">
        <div class="quick-links-card">
            <div class="quick-links-card-details">
                <div class='title'><h3>NovAScore: A New Automated Metric for Evaluating Document Level Novelty</h3>
</div>
                <div class='description'>
                    <p><span class="accented-text"><span class="body-medium">January 2025</span></span></p>
<p>We introduce NovAScore (Novelty Evaluation in Atomicity Score), an automated metric for evaluating document-level novelty. NovAScore aggregates the novelty and salience scores of atomic information, providing high interpretability and a detailed analysis of a document&#39;s novelty. With its dynamic weight adjustment scheme, NovAScore offers enhanced flexibility and an additional dimension to assess both the novelty level and the importance of information within a document.</p>
</div>
            </div>

            
                
    <a aria-label="NovAScore: A New Automated Metric for Evaluating Document Level Novelty, learn more" class="link" data-cmp-clickable data-cmp-data-layer="{&#34;event&#34;:&#34;cmp:click&#34;,&#34;webInteraction&#34;:{&#34;ctaType&#34;:&#34;link&#34;,&#34;ctaText&#34;:&#34;Read more&#34;,&#34;ctaUrl&#34;:&#34;https://arxiv.org/abs/2409.09249&#34;,&#34;ctaTitle&#34;:&#34;NovAScore: A New Automated Metric for Evaluating Document Level Novelty&#34;,&#34;ctaComponentName&#34;:&#34;Quick Links&#34;}}" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2409.09249" target="_blank">
        <span class="link-text">Read more</span>

        
            
  
  
  <span class="icon icon-16" data-icon="&#xf061"></span>
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  

        
    </a>

            
        </div>
    
        <div class="quick-links-card">
            <div class="quick-links-card-details">
                <div class='title'><h3>An Exploratory Framework for LLM-assisted Human Annotation of Speech Datasets</h3>
</div>
                <div class='description'>
                    <p><span class="accented-text"><span class="body-medium">August 2025</span></span></p>
<p>We introduce a framework for LLM-based human-in-the-loop ASR designed to enhance the quality of ASR transcripts, with a particular focus on accurately capturing named entities. A key contribution of this work is demonstrating that when LLMs are provided with high-quality, human-annotated transcript examples, even a small set can significantly improve WER and entity recall rate.</p>
</div>
            </div>

            
                
    <a aria-label="An Exploratory Framework for LLM-assisted Human Annotation of Speech Datasets, learn more" class="link" data-cmp-clickable data-cmp-data-layer="{&#34;event&#34;:&#34;cmp:click&#34;,&#34;webInteraction&#34;:{&#34;ctaType&#34;:&#34;link&#34;,&#34;ctaText&#34;:&#34;Read more&#34;,&#34;ctaUrl&#34;:&#34;https://www.isca-archive.org/interspeech_2025/johnson25_interspeech.pdf&#34;,&#34;ctaTitle&#34;:&#34;An Exploratory Framework for LLM-assisted Human Annotation of Speech Datasets&#34;,&#34;ctaComponentName&#34;:&#34;Quick Links&#34;}}" href="https://www.isca-archive.org/interspeech_2025/johnson25_interspeech.pdf" target="_blank">
        <span class="link-text">Read more</span>

        
            
  
  
  <span class="icon icon-16" data-icon="&#xf061"></span>
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  

        
    </a>

            
        </div>
    
        <div class="quick-links-card">
            <div class="quick-links-card-details">
                <div class='title'><h3>Comparison-Based Automatic Evaluation for Meeting Summarization</h3>
</div>
                <div class='description'>
                    <p><span class="accented-text"><span class="body-medium">August 2025</span></span></p>
<p>We introduce CREAM (Comparison-based Reference-free Elo-ranked Automatic evaluation for Meeting summarization), a novel framework that addresses the unique challenges of evaluating meeting summaries. CREAM leverages a combination of chain-of-thought reasoning and key facts alignment to assess conciseness and completeness of model-generated summaries without requiring reference.</p>
</div>
            </div>

            
                
    <a aria-label="Comparison-Based Automatic Evaluation for Meeting Summarization, learn more" class="link" data-cmp-clickable data-cmp-data-layer="{&#34;event&#34;:&#34;cmp:click&#34;,&#34;webInteraction&#34;:{&#34;ctaType&#34;:&#34;link&#34;,&#34;ctaText&#34;:&#34;Read more&#34;,&#34;ctaUrl&#34;:&#34;https://www.isca-archive.org/interspeech_2025/gong25c_interspeech.pdf&#34;,&#34;ctaTitle&#34;:&#34;Comparison-Based Automatic Evaluation for Meeting Summarization&#34;,&#34;ctaComponentName&#34;:&#34;Quick Links&#34;}}" href="https://www.isca-archive.org/interspeech_2025/gong25c_interspeech.pdf" target="_blank">
        <span class="link-text">Read more</span>

        
            
  
  
  <span class="icon icon-16" data-icon="&#xf061"></span>
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  

        
