        <div class="quick-links-card">
            <div class="quick-links-card-details">
                <div class='title'><h3>Systematic Evaluation of Long-Context LLMs on Financial Concepts</h3>
</div>
                <div class='description'>
                    <p><span class="accented-text"><span class="body-medium">October 2024</span></span></p>
<p>Evaluated the performance of state-of-the-art GPT-4 suite of LC LLMs in solving a series of progressively challenging tasks, as a function of factors such as context length, task difficulty, and position of key information by creating a real world financial news dataset.</p>
</div>
            </div>

            
                
    <a aria-label="Systematic Evaluation of Long-Context LLMs on Financial Concepts, opens in new tab" class="link" data-cmp-clickable data-cmp-data-layer="{&#34;event&#34;:&#34;cmp:click&#34;,&#34;webInteraction&#34;:{&#34;ctaType&#34;:&#34;link&#34;,&#34;ctaText&#34;:&#34;Read more&#34;,&#34;ctaUrl&#34;:&#34;https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.15386&#34;,&#34;ctaTitle&#34;:&#34;Systematic Evaluation of Long-Context LLMs on Financial Concepts&#34;,&#34;ctaComponentName&#34;:&#34;Quick Links&#34;}}" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.15386" target="_blank">
        <span class="link-text">Read more</span>

        
            
  
  
  <span class="icon icon-16" data-icon="&#xf061"></span>
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  
  

        
    </a>

            
        </div>
    
        <div class="quick-links-card">
            <div class="quick-links-card-details">
                <div class='title'><h3>AR-NLU: A Framework for Enhancing Natural Language Understanding Model Robustness against ASR Errors</h3>
</div>
                <div class='description'>
                    <p><span class="accented-text"><span class="body-medium">June 2024</span></span></p>
<p>A major challenge with pipeline spoken language understanding systems is that errors in the upstream automatic speech recognition (ASR) engine adversely impact downstream natural language understanding (NLU) models. To address this challenge, we propose an ASR-Robust NLU (AR-NLU) framework that extends a pre-existing NLU model by training it simultaneously on two input streams: human generated or gold transcripts and noisy ASR transcripts.</p>
</div>
            </div>

            
                
    <a aria-label="AR-NLU: A Framework for Enhancing Natural Language Understanding Model Robustness against ASR Errors, opens in new tab" class="link" data-cmp-clickable data-cmp-data-layer="{&#34;event&#34;:&#34;cmp:click&#34;,&#34;webInteraction&#34;:{&#34;ctaType&#34;:&#34;link&#34;,&#34;ctaText&#34;:&#34;Read more&#34;,&#34;ctaUrl&#34;:&#34;https://www.isca-archive.org/interspeech_2024/phung24_interspeech.html&#34;,&#34;ctaTitle&#34;:&#34;AR-NLU: A Framework for Enhancing Natural Language Understanding Model Robustness against ASR Errors&#34;,&#34;ctaComponentName&#34;:&#34;Quick Links&#34;}}" href="https://www.isca-archive.org/interspeech_2024/phung24_interspeech.html" target="_blank">
